# Execute locally

Do the step yourself when the environment allows it. Hand off only when the action needs the user's UI, secrets you cannot use, or an explicit product decision.

## Run yourself

- `git status`, `git log`, `git diff`, branch sync with `defaultBaseBranch` from `project.config.json`
- Issue/PR state via your SCM CLI or MCP (`gh`, `glab`, etc. per `PROJECT.md`)
- Issue details via tracker MCP/API documented in `PROJECT.md`
- `node .agent-workflow/tools/cli/memory.mjs bootstrap` on first turn
- Read project docs under paths in `project.config.json` (`paths.codingStandards`, etc.)

## Ask first

- Commits, push, PR create, issue tracker posts, release branches
- Destructive git or production deploys
- Scope expansion beyond the ticket
